type: software
title: "Additive-noise rigidity, a sharp growth threshold and an exact nonlinear-mixture boundary for Gaussian kernel spaces"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. For every additive noise law, a transition X' = F(x) + Z maps a Gaussian RKHS boundedly into another only if F is affine; the zero-exponential-type growth condition behind this is sharp. Finite mixtures of Gaussian branches with a common linear part are bounded exactly when each gate extends to an entire function within an explicit Gaussian growth bound: probit gates up to a threshold, logistic gates never. A several-variable Fock-space no-cancellation corollary follows."
